tip: | Look at the two tiles. | Stone on the left, water on the right, sharing one edge. Each repeats by itself, and the edge between them is a straight 2:1 stair, so either can sit beside the other.
tip: 3 | One color, then offsets. | The cobbles are one mid step with gaps one or two steps darker, and a corner a step lighter. Texture comes from moving along the ramp, not from new colors.
tip: 4 | Water is mostly one color. | A few short dashes a step lighter and darker run along the grid. They imply ripples, and leaving most of the tile flat keeps it calm.
tip: | Now repeat the stone. | Three by three, the cobbles carry on across the seams, as the pattern repeats exactly once per tile. | | seam 0 0
